redetermined  course can't be adjusted once it's begun  meaning the sorcerer has to complete the  motion even if it's no longer beneficial  now while projection sorcery normally  lasts for a second it's been shown that  with enough curse energy you can  maintain it for multiple seconds in a  row  this allows the person to continuously  build more and more momentum  reaching speeds that surpass the usual  limit of the technique  narya is the perfect example as he kept  activating it back to back during his  fight with maki resulting in him being  so fast that he literally planned to  punch through her  this is in contrast to his fight with  chozo where he only used projection  sorcery in individual bursts  so he never reached anything close to  his top speed the other benefit of this  technique is that while it's being used  anyone touched by the user's palm is  also required to move at 24 frames per  second  for most people that's an impossible  task given that they don't have  projection sorcery  so the end result is that they're frozen  in place for one second instead  those who get frozen always appear to be  stuck inside a frame and that's because  this technique is based off real life  animation  before we move on there are a few other  rules when it comes to projection  sorcery  such as the fact it doesn't allow the  sorcerer to majorly defy the laws of  physics  one example might be that you can't just  teleport from a to b without doing the  necessary motions  and it also doesn't let you do crazy  stuff like phasing through walls  if nao was to try something that insane  then he wouldn't be able to fulfill the  predetermined course of action  and if you can't do that then you end up  frozen in a frame for one second as well  final thing to mention is that when the  user is deciding which 24 movements to  perform  they can't move anywhere that's not  within their field of view the second  technique on this list is known as  construction  and compared to the last one there's a  lot more simple construction enables  maya to use curse energy to create  things out of thin air  although the objects can't be anything  too big or too complex  her go-to option has been to use it to  make bullets which is why she carries a  sick shot revolver to confuse whoever  she's up against  after six bullets have been fired anyone  who doesn't know her technique will  assume she needs to reload  giving her an opening to generate a  surprise seventh bullet to catch them  off guard  this bluff is what she used against  marky during the team battle in season 1  but the freak of nature was still able  to catch the bullet pretty quickly  a downside of construction is that it  requires a ton of crush energy to create  something  so mike could only ever produce one  bullet a day if we compare how she looks  before using her technique and  immediately afterwards the nosebleed  makes it clear this isn't an easy thing  to do  during the series the largest thing we  saw her make was this sword she made for  her sister  while she was already injured by the way  and the consequence of that was just not  great  up next we have the technique of ranta  zenin who was a member of the hay before  his untimely death  for those that don't know the hey is a  unit composed of the highest ranked  sorcerers the family has to offer  meaning he was at least semi-grade one  out of all the characters in the series  i'd say his ability is most similar to  inumaki  in that they're both able to restrict  someone using curse energy  while it's true we don't know the name  of his technique it works by focusing  his eyes on the target  and then a bigger pair of eyes manifest  next to the victim from there his  opponents are restricted  but just like her speech the  effectiveness depends on how powerful  the target is  in order to hold someone in position it  seems like he needs to keep staring at  them  and if the giant pair of eyes takes  damage then his real eyeballs also get  seriously messed up  blaze encourages the fourth technique in  this video and it was utilized by ogi  zenin who is the father to both marquis  and mai  this guy is a strong contender for worst  dad in the series and his hatred for his  children comes from the fact they  prevented him from being head of the  clan  according to ogie he was a better  sorcerer than albito in every way  with the one exception being the quality  of their children whereas nao was  perceived by everyone as a genius  maki couldn't even see curses and mai  didn't have that much cursed energy  compared to the average sorcerer  that's why in the manga he didn't feel  any sadness when trying to kill them  both  and this is where we get to his cursed  technique blazing courage enables the  user to create fire out of cursed energy  and then use that in conjunction with a  weapon  for example in chapter 148 ogi's katana  was sliced in half by maki  but by using this technique he was able  to conjure up flames to replace the part  that was broken  the following chapter he did a similar  thing only that time the flames were  way more intense and seem to be  propelled out of the katana at high  speeds  being a special grade one sorcerer you  would expect that over the years he's  used blazing courage to incinerate  hundreds of curses  which is why he was so confident in  telling maki he could burn her to the  bone  following this we have an ability  possessed by trojaroszenin who was  another member of the hay  and this technique activates when he  makes contact with the ground using  cursed energy he can manipulate the  earth to create an enormous pair of  hands which can then be made to do  anything he wants  chojiro maintains control of the hands  as long as his actual hands are touching  the floor  and like pretty much everyone else in  this video he used it to try and crush  maki like a bug  in my opinion a technique like this that  controls matter in that way  it likely has more applications than  just the big hands but no doubt this is  his preferred use of the ability  moving on we have the curse technique of  junichi zenin who was a special great  one sorcerer skilled in hand-to-hand  combat  the first time we saw this character he  attempted to uppercut naoya so it does  make sense that his special ability is  related to punching as well  this unnamed technique can manifest  several huge fists to support his own  punches  and contrary to what you might think  these fists are actually real initially  i thought they were a symbolic thing to  represent how hard he was punching but  when you look at the aftermath of his  attack there were multiple separate  craters in the ground  this implies that the fists aren't an  illusion or a metaphor of some kind  but instead they are real things  manifested from cursed energy  that makes junichi pretty destructive  overall which i guess it makes sense why  he's ranked so highly  now the final power on this list is by  far the most valuable  and that is the 10 shadows technique  this is the signature ability of the  zening clan that's been passed down for  hundreds of years  but in all that time it's never reached  its full potential users of this  technique can in theory control it to 10  different shikigami  however volume 14 confirmed that  mastering all of them hasn't been done  before  when 10 shadows first awakens in someone  that sorcerer receives a free pair of  demon dogs  but in order to control any new  shikigami they have to be exercised in a  ritual  that ritual can be started at virtually  any time by making the relevant hand  sign  as each sign creates a unique shadow  from which the spirit can emerge  the only rule of the ritual is that the  sorcerer must defeat the shikigami by  themselves  because if anyone else was to help or a  system in any way then the result would  be void so far in the series megumi has  gained control over at least five  spirits besides the demon dogs and he  can summon multiple at the same time or  even combine them using an extension of  his technique  with this extension he was able to  combine these two to create what is  essentially an 11th shikigami  and these flying toads have one  advantage over the others if this hybrid  was completely destroyed  they could still return again in the  future as long as mikumi has control  over the two needed to create it  on the other hand if any of the original  10 are wiped out then usually they won't  be able to come back  upon death their cursed energy is  inherited by the others which is why the  black demon dog was significantly  stronger after a sibling was killed  anyway in the mangrove was revealed that  a previous user of 10 shadows once  fought against someone from the gojo  clan who had the limitless curse  technique and the six eyes  those past sorcerers were each heads of  their respective families meaning  someone of gojo's level of strength  fought against someone who was likely a  stronger version of megumi  the end result was that both of them  died and for shigeru believed there was  only one chikigami that could kill  someone that powerful  the spirit in question is maharaga and  besides having a super long name it is  also the shikigami that no zenin has  been able to exercise  during its fight with sukuna we love  what made it so unbeatable as it  possesses incredible strength incredible  durability  and is able to adapt to literally  anything once the wheel in its head  makes a single turn  any attack that previously worked  against maharaga is now able to be  counted  so the only way to win is to destroy it  with a new attack before it can adjust  an example is how tsukuna initially used  his dismantle attack to slice through  the shikigami  and although it wasn't fate that it was  enough to cause significant damage  a second later the wheel turned and  maharaga had then adapted to all types  of slashing attacks  including the two different kinds that  sukun is able to do from that point  onwards it was able to either deflect  any kind of slash  or if it was unable to do that then it  would still regenerate after the attack  was over  this was proven during chapter 119 as  even after mauraga was relentlessly torn  apart by a new type of slash  it began the process of restoring itself  soon afterwards  on a few occasions fujiguru has  considered using the shigegami to kill  both himself and an enemy he doesn't  think he can beat  but it's crazy that this guy of all  people is the one he used it against  other shikigami he has include max  elephant which was able to produce so  much water from its trunk that it sent  nowatoshi bursting out of building in  season 1.  its massive size can also be used to  crush enemies although this can be  counted depending on what technique the  opponent has  rabbit escape is another shikigami but  as the name suggests it has no offensive  capabilities  and the swarm of rabbits is nearly  always used just to distract people  earlier in the video i briefly mentioned  nue but i should further explain that  besides being able to fly  its wings can deliver an electric shock  to paralyze his opponents  against sukhana this had absolutely zero  effect but naratoshi was unable to move  for a few seconds after being hit with  this  fushiguro can also use its flight for  his own movement and just like the other  shikigami he controls  he can make nue disappear whenever he  needs to moving over to the demon dogs  these guys have their own unique powers  since they can use their sense of smell  for a variety of things including  detecting nearby curses  tracking down certain people or even  tracking certain locations  toad is mainly useful for his long  tongue which most of the time is either  used to target things he wants to either  grab like when he grab nabarro or  potentially if he wants to fling someone  away or just potentially stop a certain  weapon  those can all be used with a long tongue  great serpent's fangs were useful for  biting and restricting the movement of  curses and on top of that the shadows  themselves can be used to store a  variety of weapons  meaning megumi always has options  available to him in any given situation  last thing to mention on 10 shadows is  the domain expansion which is not  something he's been able to complete as  of making this video  what i mean by that is that he's not  been able to finish the barrier that  most domains require  but on the plus side it does still  vastly improve what 10 shadows can do  with this domain he can make duplicate  versions of any shikigami  which is why two versions of nue were  seen to be attacking this cursed spirit  as we know he only has one of these in  normal circumstances so i guess if he  was to ever control maharaga  then he could make duplicate versions of  that as well beyond being able to  multiply the shikigami the most shocking  thing to me about this domain was that  he could make a shadow version of  himself  a power like that is fantastic for  bluffing so at its full potential this  domain i would say ranks in the top  three  with that said thank you for watching  this video on all zen and curse  techniques  and be sure to hit that sub button if  you haven't already until the next one  peace out

